   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThay</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nAlmost everyone who uses the <code>dsm</code>​ package has a large proportion of their segments without detections. You way wish to consider use of the Tweedie distribution to add flexibility to your modelling coming from overdispersion. The subject is briefly\r\n discussed in this case study:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://examples.distancesampling.org/dsm-line-dolphins/mexico-analysis.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://examples.distancesampling.org/dsm-line-dolphins/mexico-analysis.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472177259000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3oyEtdJzFV_vtZG3xcOlmJ\">http://examples.distancesampling.org/dsm-line-dolphins/mexico-analysis.html</a><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"width:100%;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;max-width:800px;min-width:424px\">\r\n<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"padding:12px 36px 12px 12px;width:100%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-radius:2px\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"border-spacing:0px\" valign=\"top\">\r\n<td style=\"width:100%\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:300;margin-right:8px;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px\">\r\n<a href=\"http://examples.distancesampling.org/dsm-line-dolphins/mexico-analysis.html\" style=\"text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://examples.distancesampling.org/dsm-line-dolphins/mexico-analysis.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472177259000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3oyEtdJzFV_vtZG3xcOlmJ\">Example `dsm` analysis: pantropical dolphins in the Gulf of Mexico</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;max-height:100px;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px;margin-right:8px;overflow:hidden;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">\r\nExample spatial analysis of pantropical spotted dolphins.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:400;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(166,166,166)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://examples.distancesampling.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://examples.distancesampling.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472177259000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3cn-JqlbcIZBVyXNA5xYhl\">examples.distancesampling.org</a></div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Thayusky da Penha &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">thay...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 19 April 2023 15:15<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [distance-sampling] dsm - how to deal with zero-inflation?</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">\r\nDear distance samplers,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI have successfully modelled dolphin population size using the &#39;Distance&#39; package in R.\r\n<br>\r\nAs I am using data from a very heterogeneous area in terms of oceanographic features, I&#39;ve  decided to go forward  and use the &#39;dsm&#39; package to include environmental covariates.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nHowever, I have to deal with zero inflation and I don&#39;t know how to do that using &#39;dsm&#39; (?).<br>\r\nDoes anyone have an explanation and/or solution to my question?</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">\r\n<br>\r\nWith kind regards,<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">--</span><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<div><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:x-small;color:rgb(133,90,64)\"> </span></font><span style=\"color:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;border:0px;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:Candara,Optima,sans-serif;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\"><b>Thayusky\r\n da Penha Correa</b></span><span style=\"color:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;border:0px;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:Candara,Optima,sans-serif;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\"> (she/her)</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"border:0px;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(32,33,36)\">\r\n<font color=\"#444444\" size=\"1\"><span style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:inherit\">\r\n<div style=\"font:inherit;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:inherit\">\r\n<span style=\"border:0px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:Candara,Optima,sans-serif;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:inherit\">Ph.D.\r\n student in Ecology<br>\r\nUniversidade Federal de Santa Catarina<br>\r\n<span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"></span><br>\r\n</span></div>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:HelveticaNeue-Light,&quot;Helvetica Neue Light&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,128);font-family:verdana,helvetica,sans-serif\"><font size=\"1\"><br>\r\n</font></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p></p></div></div>"
